---
code: authored-decline-class
when-fires: a verdict arm carries a report-sink emission whose `<verb> <class>` header WAS readable statically. lint/source_oracle_solo.rs, tier-1 inventory. `{class}` is the read class token.
why: 27W decline-class-emission - classing a decline is enhancement, and the inventory is how an author sees what they classed. Advisory only, never gates; the license plane never reads a class.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
foo__is_converged() {
   case "$1" in
   key) printf 'decline unsound %s is a write-only trigger key\n' "$2" >>"${DREP_V1:-/dev/null}"
        return 2 ;;
   *) return 2 ;;
   esac
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  4:9 info [oracle-declined-inventory:authored-decline-class] this verdict arm deliberately declines to answer, classed `unsound`: any site it matches is left to run, and the class only shapes Dorc's advisory hints, never what executes.

dorc lint: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 1 info across 1 file.
